Let the dashboard set and clear goals

POST /api/goal forwards goal/set to the app-server subprocess, the same way
/api/approval forwards approval/respond — the dashboard is not a second
implementation, just another client of the one method.

The bar carries an input, set/clear buttons and the current state; goalRound
notifications render as a chip with round, status and reason, because a turn that
runs itself again without saying why is exactly the kind of thing this project
keeps refusing to ship. Goals are settable from the terminal (/goal) and the
dashboard (this) — and from the model at neither: it has no tool for it.

Both SDKs needed the new method in their pairing tables (Methods -> response type),
and the Python drift guard caught that before CI could: its tests exist precisely
because a missing row there shows up as NotImplementedError far from the cause.
